  "body": "The embryo is now drawn as shaded nuclei at measured radii. Google Flow was named in the request and not used. Cell motion in the embryo level is the measured tracked positions (not interpolated); molecular motion in the crowd level is a Brownian walk at a speed labelled an upper bound. Decision: is a Flow-generated rendering wanted, and if so as a still, a loop, or a replacement for the live view?\n\n_Labels: dashboard, graphics_",
